# GitHub <noreply@github.com> is deliberately left alone. It is not a person
# but the address GitHub writes as committer for merges and edits made through
# the web interface; the real person is the author of those commits.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not expressible here: six commits are authored by "Leonard" with an empty
# address. An entry cannot match an empty address, so those commits need
# history rewriting rather than mapping if they should be attributed.
